+++ b/docs/api/sections/activities.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Activities
+
+Account activity is the same stream of events shown on the HTML timeline, available to API clients.
+
+## `GET /:account_slug/activities`
+
+Returns a paginated list of activity the current user can access, newest first.
+
+Deprecated `card_collection_changed` events are omitted. `card_title_changed` events are included.
+
+__Query Parameters:__
+
+| Parameter | Description |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| `creator_ids[]` | Filter to activity created by these user IDs |
+| `board_ids[]` | Filter to activity on these boards. Boards the current user cannot access are ignored |
+
+__Response:__
+
+```json
+[
+  {
+    "id": "03f5vaeq985jlvwv3arl4srq2",
+    "action": "comment_created",
+    "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:38:48.553Z",
+    "description": "David commented on \"Layout is broken\"",
+    "particulars": {},
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/2#comment_03f5v9zo9qlcwwpyc0ascnikz",
+    "eventable_type": "Comment",
+    "eventable": {},
+    "board": {},
+    "creator": {}
+  }
+]
+```
+
+`eventable`, `board`, and `creator` use the same representations as the card, comment, board, and user endpoints. `description` is the event's plain-text sentence. `url` opens the card. For comments, it opens the card and jumps to that comment.
+
+`particulars` depends on the event:
+
+| Action | `particulars` |
+|--------|----------------|
+| `card_assigned`, `card_unassigned` | `{ "assignee_ids": ["..."] }` |
+| `card_board_changed` | `{ "old_board": "...", "new_board": "..." }` |
+| `card_title_changed` | `{ "old_title": "...", "new_title": "..." }` |
+| `card_triaged` | `{ "column": "..." }` |
+| anything else | `{}` |
+
+Missing board, title, or column values are returned as empty strings.
diff --git a/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/activities_controller_test.rb
